{#-
  BLOCK: chrome — the connective pieces §06 does not name individually: the
  hero figure, the section/count line, the report-criteria line and the
  truncation note. One file with a `piece`, as before.

  THE HERO, as Design draws it: the one number at 46px in `ink`
  (`primary_ink`, brand as text, AA on white and on the tint by construction)
  on a `tint` panel, its label under it, and an optional sub-line. The number
  carries `tr-brand`, which the dark-mode style block points at a brand ink
  derived for the dark card — without it the number kept its light-mode
  colour on a dark panel (1.13:1 on navy, measured in the review).

  The sub-line is `#475569`, not Design's `#64748B`: on the tint `#64748B`
  measured 4.25–4.35:1 on every brand, under AA.

  `count_pill` and `section_label` are no longer a pill and a rule: one 11px
  uppercase line, the same piece Design uses above every collection.
  The old gradient `divider` is gone — Design dropped it; spacing is cell
  padding.

  THE TRUNCATION NOTE PROMISES THE REST ONLY WHERE THE PDF HAS IT. Design's
  line is "All of them are in the report", true for the catalog kinds, whose
  PDF renders every matching listing, and false for the snapshot kinds, whose
  PDF is a capped sample (`market_builder.PDF_CONFIG`). `pdf_has_all` is
  decided in Python and held to PDF_CONFIG by a test.
-#}
{% if piece == 'hero' -%}
          <tr><td class="tr-pad" style="padding:22px 28px 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;"><table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" style="border-collapse:collapse;"><tr><td class="tr-tint" bgcolor="{{ tint }}" style="padding:22px 24px;background:{{ tint }};font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;"><div class="tr-brand" style="font-size:46px;line-height:1;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.03em;color:{{ ink }};">{{ value }}</div><div class="tr-body" style="margin-top:8px;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:600;color:#334155;">{{ label }}</div>{% if sub %}<div class="tr-muted" style="margin-top:4px;font-size:13px;color:#475569;">{{ sub }}</div>{% endif %}</td></tr></table></td></tr>
{%- elif piece == 'section_label' or piece == 'count_pill' -%}
          <tr><td class="tr-pad" style="padding:28px 28px 6px;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;"><span class="tr-muted" style="font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#64748B;">{{ text }}</span></td></tr>
{%- elif piece == 'filter_blurb' -%}
          <tr><td class="tr-pad" style="padding:10px 28px 0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;"><span class="tr-muted" style="font-size:13px;line-height:1.5;color:#64748B;">{{ text }}</span></td></tr>
{%- elif piece == 'truncation_note' -%}
          <tr><td align="center" class="tr-pad" style="padding:16px 28px 0;text-align:center;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;"><span class="tr-muted" style="font-size:13px;color:#64748B;">Showing {{ showing }} of {{ total_available }}.{% if pdf_has_all %} All of them are in the report.{% endif %}</span></td></tr>
{%- endif %}
